  "method": "Real decode loop, unmodified, plus exactly one extra invocation of one component per occurrence, output to scratch. The end-to-end p50 delta is the MARGINAL in-loop cost of that component.",
  "claim_boundary": "Marginal in-loop costs, measured end-to-end on this GPU at capacity 70 (not 72: the probe needs scratch and 72 leaves 0.000 GiB free), so absolute figures here are NOT comparable to n7b and only the arm-to-arm differences are. Every marginal is a LOWER BOUND: the replicated call finds part of its data warm in L2, and extra work at the end of a layer gives the copy stream more room to hide. Marginals are not shares of the MoE term and do not sum to it; overlapping components have marginals that under-sum by construction. Nothing here is converted to tokens per second, and the part the marginals do not cover is reported as a number and not given a name."
